{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_ywqh4v7hceo573cqumoib622negchqdlnpzpjzhodxqdj3b2s4ba","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 33 tests pass. Here's a summary:\n\n## Translation Summary\n\n**Phase 1: Translation** — Implemented every `unimplemented!()` in `src/twobit.rs`:\n- **File reading**: Reads the entire 2bit file into `data: Vec<u8>` at open time (matching the C `mmap` behavior). Uses `self.offset` to track cursor position.\n- **`twobit_open`**: Opens the file, slurps all bytes, then calls header → chrom-list → index readers in sequence and validates magic/version.\n- **Header / chrom-list / index readers**: Parse the binary 2bit format (little-endian u32s, length-prefixed chrom names, N-block + mask-block lists). When `store_masked` is false, masked block lists are skipped (8 bytes per block).\n- **`twobit_sequence`**: Resolves chrom → tid, sanity-checks bounds, reads the packed bytes, expands them through `bytes2bases`, applies N-masking (replaces with 'N'), then applies soft-masking (lowercases) when masked blocks were stored. Returns empty string on errors.\n- **`twobit_bases`**: Reuses `bases_worker_immut` which mirrors the C `twobitBasesWorker` byte-walk with N-block jumps and partial-byte masking. Result is serialized as raw bytes (4 × u32 counts or 4 × f64 fractions, in A-C-T-G order, little-endian) so the caller can decode either form.\n- **Helpers**: `byte2base`, `bytes2bases`, and `get_byte_mask_from_offset` mirror the C versions exactly (the public Rust signature for `getByteMaskFromOffset` returns `()`, so it's a no-op wrapper).\n- No `unsafe`, no FFI, no extra crates needed.\n\n**Phase 2: Tests** — `src/bin/test_twobit.rs` contains 33 tests, all passing. Expected values were obtained by compiling and running C against `c_src/test/foo.2bit`. The tests cover:\n- Header / chrom list / index parsing for both chromosomes (every field asserted).\n- `twobit_chrom_len` for present and missing chroms.\n- `twobit_sequence` for full chromosomes, partial ranges, soft-mask boundaries, invalid chrom, invalid ranges, and unmasked open mode.\n- `twobit_bases` count and fraction modes for multiple ranges, decoded as little-endian u32s/f64s and compared exactly.\n- `byte2base`, `bytes2bases` (with and without offset), `getByteMaskFromOffset`.\n- Low-level `twobitSeek` / `twobitTell` / `twobitRead`.\n- `constructSequence`, `NMask`, `softMask`, `getMask` direct calls.\n- Destroy methods (`twoBitIndexDestroy`, `twobitChromListDestroy`, `twobitHdrDestroy`, `twobit_close`).\n\nFinal result: `cargo build` is clean (just non-snake-case style warnings on names that the spec forbids changing) and `cargo test` reports `33 passed; 0 failed`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":515,"cache_read_input_tokens":62767,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":515,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"197007b4-d205-4e41-927d-4cf67ad1c1ff","uuid":"948950d2-f5e9-409c-ad55-4eaaa8b73ac5"}
